---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import me2 from "../assets/arttu-2.jpg";
import me3 from "../assets/arttu-3.jpg";
import me4 from "../assets/arttu-4.jpg";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="A look behind the screen — what drives me, what I value, and what I tinker with."
  pageClass="page-red"
>
  <h1>whoami</h1>
  <p class="full-width">
    I'm Arttu - a developer from Finland with a background in computer science
    and eCommerce development. This page is a more personal look at what I do
    outside of work and what keeps me curious. While my <a href="/experience/"
      >Experience</a
    > page covers the professional side, this one's about the hobbies, interests,
    and values that shape how I think and work.
  </p>

  <hr class="hr-4" />

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>Hobbies & Interests</h2>

      <p>
        Some would say I collect hobbies, but I like to think that I'm curious
        and I just enjoy a lot of different things.
      </p>

      <p>
        Latest one is <a
          href="https://arttu.net/blog/why-and-how-i-started-my-dj-career/"
          >DJ'ing</a
        > - I started it in March 2025. Still very much in the beginner zone, but
        I've already fallen into the world of spinning decks. It's an excellent way
        to spend time: you constantly bump into good music and connect with like-minded
        people.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've also picked up <a
          href="https://arttu.net/blog/running-with-suunto-run/">running</a
        > after many, many years of pause. Slowly trying to get back into the shape
        in which I was 10 years ago.
      </p>

      <p>
        In summer I like to go <strong>magnet fishing</strong>. Low effort,
        weirdly satisfying. Feels like a treasure hunt, especially fun with
        friends.
      </p>

      <p>
        I <a href="/reading-list/">read</a>
        a lot too: mostly biographies, tech history, and the occasional strange or
        esoteric topic. When it comes to <a
          href="https://letterboxd.com/narttu/">movies and tv-shows</a
        >, it's usually sci-fi, thrillers, horror, or anime.
      </p>

      <p>
        Then there's <strong>hiking</strong>, <strong>Rubik's cube</strong>, <strong
          >puzzles</strong
        >, <strong>playing guitar</strong> and the list goes on. I won't pretend
        I do them all regularly, but they're all there from time to time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <Image src={me4} alt="Arttu as a Santa Claus." />
      <span>Arttu as a Santa Claus.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section reverse">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>Tech & Tinkering</h2>

      <p>
        I started coding as a young boy, when websites still used table layouts
        and blinking text. First projects were in pure HTML and CSS, and I built
        small games with CoolBasic. None of them survived. I kind of wish they
        did.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm into tech history: things like “why VHS beat Betamax” or “what
        killed Symbian”. I think those stories tell a lot about how humans,
        systems and decisions mix together. I've also researched obscure
        programming languages in my
        <a
          href="https://jyx.jyu.fi/handle/123456789/81727"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Bachelor's Thesis</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've messed around with different OSes, run a home Linux server, and
        started countless side projects. Many based on a joke. Most unfinished.
        Fun while they lasted. Some of the ones that were completed can be found
        from my <a href="/projects/">projects</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Nowadays I don't have that much time for fun side-projects, since I'm
        working and studying at the same time. Most of my free time around
        computers is spent on this site and research about new tech and AI
        tools. In this industry, staying curious and up-to-date is half the
        battle.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <Image src={me2} alt="Arttu as an Elf" />
      <span>Arttu as an elf.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>What I Value</h2>
      <p>
        I like figuring things out: be that in tech, people, systems or stories.
        I prefer out-of-the-box thinking and learning by doing, after getting
        just enough background to jump in.
      </p>
      <p>
        I admire people who are genuinely into things. Doesn't matter what:
        sports, insects, obscure programming languages. The weirder the better.
        Passion is cool.
      </p>
      <p>
        I respect people who treat others as people regardless of title, role,
        or status. Staying grounded and human matters, both in everyday life and
        professional setting.
      </p>
      <p>
        And lastly, I like good vibes and try to make everyday situation more
        fun - maybe too much sometimes. Still figuring out the good balance of
        serious and playful. Good example of that is this page: the sections
        could have gone without the christmas photos altogether, but where's the
        fun in that? Me smiling psychotically as different christmas charactes
        is way more memorable. Plus, they fit almost perfectly to the colors of
        the site!
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <Image src={me3} alt="Arttu as a reindeer" />
      <span>Arttu as a reindeer.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="hr-3" />

  <p>
    If any of this feels familiar, you'll probably enjoy my <a href="/blog/"
      >blog</a
    >.
  </p>

  <style>
    /* ===== Layout keeps your two-column structure ===== */
    .about-section {
      position: relative;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 4rem;

      /* poster card styling */
      background: var(--accent-second);
      color: var(--color-text-dark);
      border: 3px solid var(--color-outlines-dark);
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 1.35rem;
    }

    /* red spine bar on top */
    .about-section::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: -3px;
      right: -3px;
      top: -3px;
      height: 10px;
      background: var(--accent);
    }

    /* reversed rows still work */
    .about-section.reverse {
      direction: rtl;
    }
    .about-section.reverse > * {
      direction: ltr;
    }

    /* text + links on cream (on-paper rules) */
    .about-text {
      max-width: 65ch;
    }
    .about-text p {
      margin: 0.65rem 0;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .about-text a {
      color: var(--color-text-dark);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: var(--color-text-dark);
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
    .about-text a:hover {
      text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    }

    /* section titles inside the card */
    .about-text h2 {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      color: var(--color-text-dark);
      margin: 0.2rem 0 0.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    }

    /* tiny red “stamp” before the title (keeps your emojis; stamp sits before them) */
    .about-text h2::before {
      content: "";
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
      background: var(--accent);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-outlines-dark);
      display: inline-block;
    }

    /* any lists inside about text */
    .about-text ul {
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
      padding-left: 1.1rem;
    }
    .about-text li {
      margin: 0.3rem 0;
      list-style: none;
      position: relative;
    }
    .about-text li::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: -1.1rem;
      top: 0.6em;
      width: 0.5rem;
      height: 0.5rem;
      background: var(--color-outlines-dark);
    }

    /* visual column */
    .about-image {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 100%;
    }

    /* enter animation (kept) */
    .about-image {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(20px) scale(0.95);
      transition: all 0.6s ease-out;
    }
    .about-image.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
    }

    .about-image span {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--color-text-dark);
      opacity: 0.7;
      text-align: left;
    }

    /* mobile */
    @media (max-width: 980px) {
      .about-section,
      .about-section.reverse {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        direction: ltr;
        gap: 1.25rem;
        padding: 1rem 1rem 1.1rem;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
      }
      .about-image {
        margin-top: 0;
        min-height: auto;
        height: auto;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("visible");
        }
      });
    },
    {
      threshold: 0.6,
    }
  );

  document.querySelectorAll(".about-image").forEach((el) => {
    observer.observe(el);
  });
</script>
